= afternoon
>>> fade in
(After school...)

(Monospace text flies past the screen.)
> ...I'm in the school's security system.
(A moment's pause.)
> And the local internet junctions.
> If she's working with Edison, I'll probably be able to escape, but I need to be careful.
> Everything seems normal. Though, of course, they could be covering their tracks in the same way I do.
> I'll keep an eye on things.

(In the PHO club room...)

mauve: Wow, you actually showed up.
cipher: Yes, is there a reason you didn't expect me to?
mauve: I thought I had botched that whole conversation, to be honest.
cipher: You're not wrong.
(You take a deep breath.)
cipher: What is this really about?
(Her face is stony.)
cipher: You clearly wanted to get me on my own. Why?
(A moment's pause.)
mauve: I want you to know. If you tell anyone about this, I have ways to make you regret it.
cipher: ...Huh? Yeah, I guess I can keep a secret.
(A moment's pause.)
mauve: I can read minds.
cipher: ...I'm going to need proof.
mauve: That's the problem. You're the only person I've ever met that I can't read at all. But, uh... Just so you know I'm not full of shit.
(She points two fingers at her water bottle. Unprompted, the cap pops open, and its contents snake out into the air. She waggles her finger, and the water breaks up into a smattering of droplets before she directs it back into the container.)
cipher: Huh. I guess I shouldn't be surprised that that's possible, given what I've been through.
> And if she can really read minds... I certainly wasn't expecting anything like that to break my cover.
mauve: I want to know why I can't hear you.
cipher: ...I have a pretty good idea why. The same goes for this, though - you can't tell a soul, and I can give you a very good reason not to if it comes to that.
mauve: Of course, I figured it'd be something like that.
(You speak matter-of-factly.)
cipher: I'm an android.
(Mauve's eyes widen.)
cipher: Before you ask: no, I'm not some sloppy stochastic parrot. I have no idea how I'm conscious, but I am, as far as I can tell. As for proof-?
(You issue a command to the nanite sludge that fills your circulatory system. There's a tingle in your forearm as it separates the skin and pulls back from the seam, then a click as the latch disengages. Your hand goes numb, dropping onto the table.)
(With your remaining hand, you pick it up and show her the socket.)
cipher: That should be sufficient.
(She looks a little queasy.)
mauve: Oh.
> Somehow, I feel slighted.
cipher: ...Sorry to disappoint.
(You slot your hand back into place.)
mauve: Well. Now I know.
cipher: And now we're even.
(She nods sagely.)
mauve: Mutually assured destruction.

>>> confidant mauve 1

(You stand to leave.)
mauve: Hang on.
cipher: Hmm?
mauve: Do you think we could keep meeting up anyway?
cipher: All right, why?
mauve: I've never been able to talk in-person like this without hearing things I shouldn't.
(She averts her eyes.)
mauve: ...It's nice.

